  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Invest the exact same hundred dollars a month, but start at four different ages. The final results are almost unfair.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "$100 a month.",
            "4 start ages."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Start at twenty, and by sixty-five you could be sitting on well over half a million dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "$100/mo until 65",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "20",
              "name": "Start at 20",
              "value": "~$560K",
              "note": "time did the work",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 1.0
            },
            {
              "rank": "30",
              "name": "Start at 30",
              "value": "~$230K",
              "note": "still huge",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.45
            },
            {
              "rank": "40",
              "name": "Start at 40",
              "value": "~$95K",
              "note": "shrinking fast",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.2
            },
            {
              "rank": "50",
              "name": "Start at 50",
              "value": "~$35K",
              "note": "too little time",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 0.08
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Compound interest means the early money has the most time to multiply.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-compound",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · compound interest"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Notice the brutal part. Starting twenty years later doesn't cut your result in half. It guts it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Late = gutted",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "clock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Over forty years, you'd only pay in about forty-eight thousand dollars of your own money.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "$48K in",
          "label": "becomes many times more",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "These numbers assume long-run S&P 500-style returns.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-sp500",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · S&P 500"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Even twenty-five dollars a month, started at twenty-five, can grow to around ninety thousand.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "$90K",
          "label": "from just $25/month",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Steadily drip-feeding money in is dollar cost averaging.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-dca",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · dollar cost averaging"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Time, not talent, is the single most valuable asset you have in all of investing.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Time > talent",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A dollar today is worth more than a dollar decades from now.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-timevalue",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · time value of money"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So the real question isn't how much. It's when did you start?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
          "art": "bank",
          "line": "When did you start?",
          "sub": "Comment your age"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s11"
    }
  ]
